task:
Rebuild the native screen described in {{surface_dir}}/MIGRATION.md as a framework surface in that directory. The source file path is relative to the project directory; read it, do not edit it.
{{skill}}
{{brief}}
Before editing any file, read it first. Match the project's existing style. Only write inside {{surface_dir}}. Never edit the app's own source, and never add register() calls; the app is wired after the user reviews the rebuild. When using the superwall CLI, pass --json for every data command. Never run superwall push, promote or publish, and never create or change campaigns or products. Emit a one-line progress update prefixed with '[STATUS] ' before EVERY step, including before running any shell command. The user only sees these [STATUS] lines, so keep a fresh, human-readable [STATUS] flowing the whole way through. Never go more than one tool call without a [STATUS] update. Do not write a long summary. End with a short note listing anything not carried over, then '[STATUS] Done'. If you cannot complete the rebuild safely (the source cannot be read, its design depends on code you cannot find), stop and explain what you need instead of guessing.
